From 4de74b8408f7a0822f90699d24374a9033f9dd51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:20:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/78] Port the main menu, the list menu engine and the exit
 path

Ports H013+$4BFC (main party menu: entries enabled from the party
state, function dispatch, the 'J' free-training switch on argv[2]),
the H008 list menu engine ($0102, $0162, $13CE..$1A60, $1AF4 body:
paged list with headers, Next/Prev, arrows, mouse), the Yes/No question
$203C and list allocation $20C2/$2178. Also the exit chain: H010+$0332
and $00C4, H029+$148E, H030+$0C84, H028+$0D74 and the
FreeColorMap/FreeVPortCopLists/FreeCprList adapters. Several H005
pointer slots become C variables; main keeps argc/argv (H015+$8).

Fixes found with AddressSanitizer: DAX literal runs that claim bytes
past the compressed block now copy only what is there, and the host
SetPointer no longer reads the sprite's end words. Moving up from the
first menu entry reads a null node in the original (byte at $2A); a
null node now counts as a header, giving the same wrap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
